p consumer cyclical business with a $8.5B market cap on $3M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -81% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -50% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $612M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 10.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 6267% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 30041% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (95% sell ratio, net $1186.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 175% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Notice of AUR Investigation Reminder: Kessler Topaz Meltzer & Check, LLP Encourages Aurora Innovation, Inc. (AUR) Investors to Contact the Firm","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/notice-of-aur-investigation-reminder-kessler-topaz-meltzer--check-llp-encourages-aurora-innovation-inc-aur-investors-to-contact-the-firm-302938194.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794513240.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"AUR Investor Notification: Aurora Investigated for Securities Fraud on behalf of Investors with Losses after Production Delays Lead to 13% Stock Drop","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/aur-investor-notification-aurora-investigated-for-securities-fraud-on-behalf-of-investors-with-losses-after-production-delays-lead-to-13-stock-drop-302934216.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794309420.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Mirae Asset Global Investments Co